  "body": "## Source-only HOLD \u2014 do not merge or deploy\n\nThe Chairman's Sovereign Auction and Funding Pressure program needs an observed-context display in the active Terminal product. Source inspection showed that the initially proposed NeuralWebStrip parent is dormant; this change mounts a single independent leaf in the actual TerminalShell detail surface after its existing actions.\n\n### Changes\n\n- Extend the existing `/api/nw` allowlist with one fixed Macro calendar selector, caller-cookie relay, redirect refusal, timeout and private/no-store handling. The existing guarded Macro origin retains registration and staged entitlement authority.\n- Strictly validate the producer's point-in-time clocks at microsecond precision, instruments, lifecycle and context/research authority. Session changes clear context and invalidate in-flight replies.\n- Render readable EN/ZH event summaries, exact grouped decimal dollars, UTC deadlines, explicit unknowns, bounded lists and native source disclosures.\n- Preserve SignalButton, Oracle, copilot, replay, chart/analysis and exit authority. NeuralWebStrip is unchanged; no dormant risk feed is revived.\n\n### Evidence\n\n- **42 Vitest tests passed**: 8 model, 17 route and 17 React tests. **TypeScript passed**.\n- Changed leaf/presentation/E2E lint passed. Existing Shell lint remains **54 errors/14 warnings**; exact diagnostic/source-range normalization shows no added diagnostic. This is not a whole-file lint pass.\n- **18/18 actual `/terminal` Chromium cases passed**, zero skipped/flaky/unexpected cases. Three sizes, EN/ZH, real shared/full fixtures, source details, expansion, failure/unknown states and entitlement loss are covered; final screenshots were inspected.\n- Existing SignalButton text and dormant-feed absence remain invariant in the browser scenarios.\n- Start with [`SOURCE_DELIVERY.md`](https://github.com/mastermindx-market-intelligence/mastermind-terminal/blob/7993cf052d861c455274e8fe79dffc83b72f1bcd/research/sovereign_auction_context/SOURCE_DELIVERY.md); final hashes are in `VERIFIED_SOURCE_MANIFEST.json` and evidence under `verification/browser_final/`.\n\n### Boundaries and integration\n\nMacro **#8657** owns the source/economic/research vertical. The source census preserves the other held Terminal writers; the latest main script-rename import and helper call must remain together during integration. The auction mount does not overlap those hunks.\n\nTerminal remains dark-only; the light-attribute probe is diagnostic. Browser auth/CSP use declared loopback fixtures and do not certify production entitlement or CSP. A real anonymous Macro calendar request was denied, but no entitled production artifact read or deployment is claimed. No public-R2 fallback, service credential, new risk probability, sizing or exit decision is introduced.\n",
